# Only the paths below have owners; everything else needs the usual review.
#
# .github/chainguard/ holds octo-sts trust policies: each decides which CI jobs
# get a GitHub App token for this repository, and with what permissions. Merging
# one is granting CI access, so these entries request infrastructure-critical's
# review of the policies and of this file. They don't require it: main's
# ruleset needs no approvals and no code owner review, so a policy change can
# merge without that team. Requiring code owner review there would make it
# binding.
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @loyaltylion/infrastructure-critical
/.github/chainguard/    @loyaltylion/infrastructure-critical
